We examine the existence of a weak solution to the following problem:
\begin{equation*}
\begin{cases}
-\text{div}\left(a(x)\left|u\right|^{p(x)-2}u\right|^{q(x)}\left|u\right|^{p(x)}\right|^{m(x)-2}\left|u\right|^{m(x)}\right)=\lambda f(x,u) & \text{in } \Omega, \\
\left|u\right|^{p(x)}\left|u\right|^{q(x)}\left|u\right|^{m(x)}\rightarrow 0 & \text{as } x\rightarrow \partial \Omega,
\end{cases}
\end{equation*}
where $\Omega$ is a bounded domain within a complete Riemannian manifold, $p, q, m$ are functions with values in $[1, \infty)$, and $a$ is a bounded function with values in $[0, \infty)$.
